First of all, the most common classical technique for representing text is a bag‐of‐words approach, where documents are represented as vectors of size equal to the dataset vocabulary, encoding the presence or absence of vocabulary terms. This technique that is used in many NLP and Information Retrieval (IR) applications represents documents or sentences as a multiset of their words, disregarding any grammar and word order. A possible addition to this is the use of n‐grams,

